{
  "dom_id": "step-q33312",
  "name": "Question 2",
  "problem": "Find an equation of the plane that contains the point $Q(3,2,2)$ and is perpendicular to the vector $n=\u27e82,2,3\u27e9.$",
  "worked_solution": "First, notice that the position vector of $Q$ is $q=\u27e83,2,2\u27e9,$ $n=\u27e82,2,3\u27e9$ is normal to the plane.\n\nThe equation of the plane that passes though the point $Q({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})$ and is perpendicular to the vector $n$ can be given as\n\n$$\n(r-q)\\cdot n=0,\n$$\n\nwhere $r$ is the position vector of any point on the plane, and $q$ is the position vector of $Q.$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(r-q)\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ r\\cdot n-q\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ r\\cdot n & =q\\cdot n \\\\ r\\cdot \u27e82,2,3\u27e9 & =\u27e83,2,2\u27e9\\cdot \u27e82,2,3\u27e9 \\\\ r\\cdot \u27e82,2,3\u27e9 & =16.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
